4.\nReferences\n\nGarrison, P.: *Flying Without Wings: A Flight Simulation Manual.* Tab Books Inc. (Blue Ridge Summit, PA), 1985.\n\nEvans, D. C.: \"Computer Generated Images for Aircraft Use,\" *Extending the Scope of Flight Simulation.* The Royal Aeronautical Society (London), 1978.\n\nPeterson, L.; and Fenrick, C. J.: \"Vertical Motion Simulator,\" *Information Bulletin.* NASA (Moffett Field), 1984.\n\nWhizin, G. S.: \"Flight Simulation,\" *Information Bulletin.* NASA (Moffett Field), 1983.\n\nShowalter, T. W.: *Simulator Certification Methods and the Vertical Motion Simulator.* Computer Sciences Corp. (Mountain View), 1981.\n\nJones, A.D.: *Operations Manual: Vertical Motion Simulator (VMS) S.08.* NASA (Moffett Field), 1980.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFlying Without Wings by Milton O. Thompson | Open Library (https://openlibrary.org/books/OL8473024M/Flying_Without_Wings)\nciteturn15search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 27.6 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; \"By the late 1950s a small group of National Air and Space Administration (NASA) engineers and pilots were designing oddly shaped, wingless aircraft known as lifting bodies. ... Flying without wings: NASA lifting bodies and the birth of the space shuttle 1999, Smithsonian Institution Press in English  | ... ## Book Details\n\nAn edition of Flying without wings (1999)\n\n# Flying Without Wings\n\n## by Milton O. Thompson\n\nFlying Without Wings\n\nMilton O. Thompson, Milton O. ...\n\n\nLast edited by MARC Bot\n\nApril 29, 2025 | History\n\nEdit\n\n\"By the late 1950s a small group of National Air and Space Administration (NASA) engineers and pilots were designing oddly shaped, wingless aircraft known as lifting bodies. Their goal was to develop a vehicle that could survive the heat of reentry into the atmosphere, fly at subsonic speeds, and make controlled, horizontal landings, much like an airplane. But NASA, determined to beat the Soviets to the moon, adopted the more easily implemented Mercury capsules. The proponents of lifting bodies continued during the 1960s and 1970s to refine and test the concept. Their research eventually became central to the design of the space shuttle, which first flew in 1981.\"\n\nPublish Date\n\nApril 1, 1999\n\nPublisher\n\nCrecy Publishing\n\nLanguage\n\nEnglish\n\nPages\n\n248\n\n\nEdition  | Availability\n--- | ---\nFlying without wings: NASA lifting bodies and the birth of the space shuttle 1999, Smithsonian Institution Press in English  | \n\n  * Borrow\n    * Listen\n    * Locate\nFlying Without Wings April 1, 1999, Crecy Publishing Hardcover in English  | \n\n  * Locate\n\n## Book Details\n\n* * *\n\n### The Physical Object\n\nFormat\n    Hardcover\nNumber of pages\n    248\nDimensions\n    9 x 6 x 1 inches\nWeight\n    1.2 pounds\n\n### Edition Identifiers\n\nOpen Library\n    OL8473024M\nISBN 10\n    0947554785\nISBN 13\n    9780947554781\n\n### Work Identifiers\n\nWork ID\n    OL1994110W\n\n### Source records\n\n  * Harvard University record\n\n## Community Reviews (0)\n\nNo community reviews have been submitted for this work.\n\n+ Log in to add your community review\n\n## Lists\n\nDownload catalog record: RDF / JSON / OPDS | Wikipedia citation\n\n## Wikipedia citation\n\n×Close\n\nCopy and paste this code into your Wikipedia page. Need help?\n\n{{cite book|author=Milton O. Thompson |date=April 1, 1999 |orig-date=1999 |title=Flying Without Wings |publisher=Crecy Publishing |isbn=978-0-947554-78-1 |oclc=40980507 |ol=8473024M}}\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBook Review: ‘Flying Without Wings: Before the space shuttle: testing NASA’s wingless aircraft’ by Milton O Thompson and Curtis Peebles | Royal Air Force (https://www.raf.mod.uk/what-we-do/centre-for-air-and-space-power-studies/air-and-space-power-review/aspr-index/book-review-flying-without-wings-before-the-space-shuttle-testing-nasas-wingless-aircraft-by-milton-o-thomps